.TH KINTSUGI-REWIND 1 "2026-10-22" "kintsugi 0.8.0" "Kintsugi Manual"
.SH NAME
kintsugi-rewind \- rewind to a checkpoint
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kintsugi rewind
<id> <ckpt-id>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Mark a session as rewound to a checkpoint. The checkpoint becomes the resume
history.
.SH EXAMPLES
Rewind to a checkpoint:
.PP
  $ kintsugi rewind abc123 ckpt-456
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kintsugi (1),
.BR kintsugi-checkpoint (1),
.BR kintsugi-session (1)
